<http://data.silknow.org/object/d6863400-d43a-3c7f-8971-8beba85acb50/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "This textile is a ‘kesa’, the rectangular garment worn by Japanese Buddhist priests. Kesa are made of a sewn patchwork of cloth, the arrangement of the sections of fabric into columns surrounded by a border serving as a mandala, a symbolic rendering of the universe. The act of sewing the garment is in itself a devotional pursuit. This detail of the kesa shows how the sections of fabric have been almost perfectly aligned so as not to disrupt the elegant design of grapevines."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d6863400-d43a-3c7f-8971-8beba85acb50> .

