        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Buddhist priest's mantle (<i>kesa</i>) of gauze silk with design of grape vines, lined with satin silk with peonies and scrolling leaves."@en , "Kesa (Buddhist priest’s robe), polychrome figured gauze silk, lined with figured satin silk, probably woven in Kyoto, Japan, 1800-1880"@en , "This textile is a ‘kesa’, the rectangular garment worn by Japanese Buddhist priests. Kesa are made of a sewn patchwork of cloth, the arrangement of the sections of fabric into columns surrounded by a border serving as a mandala, a symbolic rendering of the universe. The act of sewing the garment is in itself a devotional pursuit. This detail of the kesa shows how the sections of fabric have been almost perfectly aligned so as not to disrupt the elegant design of grapevines."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/95f05b0a-17ba-3672-bcc8-d447e260ea53> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/cd3a09d7-c3e9-3dbf-be8a-021dde72df57> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/04bb033f-5d1f-348f-a500-4e46c807fba5> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This textile is a ‘kesa’, the rectangular garment worn by Japanese Buddhist priests. Kesa are made of a sewn patchwork of cloth, the arrangement of the sections of fabric into columns surrounded by a border serving as a mandala, a symbolic rendering of the universe. The act of sewing the garment is in itself a devotional pursuit. This detail of the kesa shows how the sections of fabric have been almost perfectly aligned so as not to disrupt the elegant design of grapevines."@en , "Kesa (Buddhist priest’s robe), polychrome figured gauze silk, lined with figured satin silk, probably woven in Kyoto, Japan, 1800-1880"@en , "Buddhist priest's mantle (<i>kesa</i>) of gauze silk with design of grape vines, lined with satin silk with peonies and scrolling leaves."@en ;
